## Batched Concurrent Inference

### Architecture
Without concurrency: each self-play game runs MCTS sequentially, one neural-net eval per sim.
With concurrency: multiple games run on threads; NN evals are batched and dispatched together.

Speedup: 3-10x depending on batch fill rate and model size.

### Config (train.json::training.selfplay_concurrency)

```json
"selfplay_concurrency": {
  "enabled": true,
  "evaluator": {
    "batch_size": 100,
    "batch_timeout_us": 30,
    "max_queue_size": 256,
    "intra_op_num_threads": 1,
    "providers": []
  }
}
```

| Field | Tuning guidance |
|-------|----------------|
| batch_size | Match to episodes_per_step or lower. Higher = better GPU utilization but higher latency. |
| batch_timeout_us | Microseconds to wait for batch fill. 30 is aggressive (good for many concurrent games). Raise to 100-500 if few games. |
| max_queue_size | 256 is safe. Raise if you see "queue full" warnings. |
| intra_op_num_threads | 1 for CPU inference (ONNX default parallelism per op). Raise for large models. |
| providers | Empty = CPU. Add "CUDAExecutionProvider" for GPU. |

### CLI flags
```bash
# Standard training
python3 -m training.cli --game splendor --output runs/splendor_run --workers 4

# With GPU provider
python3 -m training.cli --game splendor --output runs/splendor_run --workers 100 --providers cuda,cpu
```

### Opponent pool with concurrency
```json
"selfplay_concurrency": {
  "enabled": true,
  "opponent_pool_max_distinct": 3,
  "evaluator": { ... }
}
```
`opponent_pool_max_distinct`: max ONNX models loaded simultaneously. Each model gets its own inference batch queue. Memory usage scales linearly.

### Batched Inference Internals

**BatchedBeliefEvaluator**: mirrors `BatchedPolicyValueEvaluator` but for belief
net inference. Configured via the same `selfplay_concurrency.evaluator` block.
Automatically instantiated when `belief_model_path` is set and
`selfplay_concurrency.enabled` is true. Shares the batch-timeout / queue-size
knobs with the PV evaluator.

**EvaluatorPool**: manages multiple `BatchedPolicyValueEvaluator` instances (one
per distinct model path). `get_or_create(model_path)` deduplicates so concurrent
arena and opponent-pool games that reference the same checkpoint share a single
GPU/ONNX session. Used internally by the selfplay runner and arena runner.

**Hot-swap**: `MctsPVHeuristic::replace_evaluator(new_ptr)` swaps the underlying
evaluator pointer without re-creating the heuristic object. Used during training
when a new model checkpoint is exported to ONNX — the pipeline hot-swaps the
evaluator rather than tearing down and re-loading the full ONNX session from
scratch. The old evaluator is released after all in-flight sims drain.

